  "honest_summary": "Tier 1: the analog PNN draws ~54.3 mW vs ~1458.5 mW for a continuous watt-class SoC pipeline (ratio 27.3x) and ~477.8 mW for a lean edge-NPU pipeline (ratio 8.9x). The advantage survives the edge-NPU comparison because the PNN removes the shared continuous front end (ADC + DSP, ~349.8 mW) that no digital classifier choice avoids. Under a fair duty-cycled digital baseline the PNN saves energy only above a crossover duty d* = 1.47% (CI [0.97, 2.13]). Endurance gains are class-dependent and EXTEND native endurance; no 30-day continuous mission is claimed for a ~1-day AUV."
